---
// /privacy — a plain privacy notice (28 Aug, owner: "not fancy formatting
// … just a simple privacy policy"). One readable column, site voice, no
// decoration. Every claim in it is checked against what the site actually
// does: a Formspree form, Vercel hosting, Google-served fonts, one
// sessionStorage flag, no analytics, no cookies of our own. Keep this
// page truthful when the stack changes — if analytics or new processors
// ever arrive, this page updates in the same commit.
import Base from "../layouts/Base.astro";
import Header from "../components/Header.astro";
import Footer from "../components/Footer.astro";
---

<Base
  title="Privacy — Talon Insights"
  description="How Talon Insights handles the personal information you send through this site — what’s collected, why, where it goes, and your rights."
  path="/privacy"
  schema={{
    "@context": "https://schema.org",
    "@type": "WebPage",
    "@id": "https://taloninsights.co.uk/privacy#page",
    url: "https://taloninsights.co.uk/privacy",
    name: "Privacy — Talon Insights",
    about: { "@id": "https://taloninsights.co.uk/#business" },
  }}
>
  <Header />
  <main class="pv">
    <div class="pv-wrap">
      <p class="t-micro eyebrow">PRIVACY</p>
      <h1 class="pv-h1">Privacy notice</h1>
      <p class="pv-updated t-mono">LAST UPDATED — 28 AUGUST 2026</p>

      <h2>Who I am</h2>
      <p>
        Talon Insights is run by Talon Herring, based in Telford, Shropshire. I build
        websites and software for local businesses. For anything in this notice —
        questions, requests, complaints — contact me directly:
      </p>
      <p>
        Email: <a href="mailto:taloninsights@gmail.com">taloninsights@gmail.com</a><br />
        Phone: <a href="tel:+447742082423">07742 082423</a>
      </p>

      <h2>What I collect, and when</h2>
      <p>
        The only personal information this site collects is what you choose to send
        through the enquiry form: your name, your business name, a phone number or
        email address, and whatever you tell me about your project. There are no
        accounts, no sign-ups and no mailing lists.
      </p>
      <p>
        If you phone or email me directly, I’ll hold the details you give me the same
        way — to deal with your enquiry and nothing else.
      </p>

      <h2>Why I use it</h2>
      <p>
        To reply to you, arrange a call or a visit, and put together a scope and a
        price if we get that far. That’s the whole list. The lawful basis is that
        you’ve asked me to — taking steps at your request before entering into a
        contract, and my legitimate interest in answering people who contact me. I
        don’t use your details for marketing, and I don’t sell or share them with
        anyone for their own purposes.
      </p>

      <h2>Where it goes</h2>
      <p>
        A few services help run this site, and each handles some data as part of
        doing its job:
      </p>
      <p>
        <strong>Formspree</strong> processes the enquiry form and forwards what you
        submit to my email. <strong>Vercel</strong> hosts the site, and like any web
        host keeps standard server logs (such as IP addresses) for security and
        reliability. <strong>Google Fonts</strong> serves the site’s typefaces, which
        means your browser requests the font files from Google’s servers when a page
        loads. None of these are given your form details for their own use.
      </p>

      <h2>Cookies and tracking</h2>
      <p>
        This site sets no cookies and runs no analytics or advertising trackers. It
        uses one small piece of browser storage — a flag that prevents an old
        redirect from looping — which contains nothing personal and never leaves
        your browser.
      </p>

      <h2>How long I keep it</h2>
      <p>
        Enquiries are kept for as long as it takes to deal with them, and for a
        reasonable period afterwards in case you come back. If we work together,
        your details become part of normal business records and are kept for as
        long as the law requires. If you’d like an enquiry deleted sooner, ask and
        I’ll do it.
      </p>

      <h2>Your rights</h2>
      <p>
        Under UK data protection law you can ask me for a copy of the personal
        information I hold about you, ask for it to be corrected or deleted, object
        to or restrict how it’s used, and ask for it in a portable format. Email me
        and I’ll sort it — there’s no form or process, it’s one person reading one
        inbox.
      </p>
      <p>
        If you’re not happy with how I’ve handled your information, you have the
        right to complain to the Information Commissioner’s Office at
        <a href="https://ico.org.uk" rel="noopener">ico.org.uk</a>.
      </p>

      <h2>Changes</h2>
      <p>
        If how this site handles information changes, this page changes with it,
        and the date at the top tells you when.
      </p>
    </div>
  </main>
  <Footer />
</Base>

<style>
  .pv { background: var(--color-ink-deep); }
  .pv-wrap {
    max-width: 46em;
    margin-inline: auto;
    padding: 140px 24px 110px;
  }
  .pv-h1 {
    margin-top: 14px;
    font-family: var(--font-display);
    font-weight: 600;
    font-size: clamp(2.25rem, 3vw, 3.5rem);
    line-height: 1.08;
    letter-spacing: -0.02em;
    color: var(--color-sheet);
  }
  .pv-updated {
    margin-top: 14px;
    font-size: 0.9375rem;
    letter-spacing: 0.12em;
    color: rgb(245 247 249 / 0.45);
  }
  .pv h2 {
    margin-top: 44px;
    font-family: var(--font-display);
    font-weight: 600;
    font-size: 1.5rem;
    color: var(--color-sheet);
  }
  .pv p {
    margin-top: 16px;
    font-size: 1.1875rem;
    line-height: 1.7;
    color: rgb(245 247 249 / 0.75);
  }
  .pv strong { color: var(--color-sheet); font-weight: 600; }
  .pv a {
    color: var(--color-cobalt-lift);
    text-decoration: none;
    border-bottom: 1px solid rgb(77 124 255 / 0.45);
    transition: color 180ms var(--ease), border-color 180ms var(--ease);
  }
  .pv a:hover { color: var(--color-sheet); border-color: rgb(245 247 249 / 0.5); }
</style>
